# REAL FEATURE, completed 2026-08-24: network vulnerability scanning via
# GVM/OpenVAS. The gvm-helper talks to gvmd over its unix socket, which is
# root-owned inside a docker volume, so the helper must run as root.
#
# REAL BUG THIS FIXES: GvmClient used to SSH to 127.0.0.1 to run the helper.
# That hop had never worked -- no private key existed for administrator and
# 127.0.0.1 was not in known_hosts -- so no scan had ever run on this platform.
# The client now invokes the helper directly, which needs this grant.
#
# Granted to ADMINISTRATOR, not www-data: the queue worker runs as
# administrator (obaits-queue.service), and RunScan is a queued job. Web
# requests never invoke this path.
#
# Scoped to the one helper script by absolute path. A relative path here would
# be a privilege-escalation hole.
administrator ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/python3 /var/www/obaits/ops/gvm-helper/gvm_run.py *
